# Implementation Plan: General Pages

This plan structures the implementation of the 12 General/Shared Pages (G1–G12) defined in the [handee-web-pages-spec.md](file:///d:/SLIIT/Year%203%20Semester%201/SE3090%20-%20Software%20Engineering%20Frameworks/Assignment/handee/web/docs/handee-web-pages-spec.md). The design will strictly follow the Minimal & Clean aesthetic, promoting Trust and Confidence.

## User Review Required
Please review the phases below. Does this ordering make sense to you? Would you like to start building Phase 2 (Core Application Shell & Errors) immediately after approval?

## Proposed Phased Plan

### Phase 2: Core Application Shell & Error Boundaries
Establishing the foundational routing so all future development runs smoothly.
- **Routing Infrastructure**: Implement React Router with Auth-Guarded layouts (Protected vs Public routes).
- **App Shell (G6)**: Build out the main `/dashboard` Shell layout. This serves as the post-login shell combining the Sidebar/Top navigation adapted to the user's role (Admin, Provider, Customer).
- **Error Boundaries (G10, G11, G12)**: Implement standard fallback screens for Not Found (404), Unauthorized (403), and Server Error (`/error`), applying our new clean aesthetic.

### Phase 3: Authentication & Onboarding
Creating the public entry points for users.
- **Login (G2)**: Clean form for email/password, handling JWT issuance and intelligent redirecting.
- **Customer Registration (G3)**: Simple onboarding flow for users.
- **Provider Registration (G4)**: Provider initial sign-up that seamlessly hands off to the main verification workflow component.
- **Password Recovery (G5)**: The Forgot and Reset password forms.

### Phase 4: Public Landing Page
- **Landing / Marketing (G1)**: The absolute root (`/`). A highly polished, trust-inspiring public page highlighting the value proposition for both customers and tradespeople with clear CTAs.

### Phase 5: Shared Authenticated Features
- **Account Settings (G7)**: Unified settings panels for managing personal info, password changes, and notification preferences.
- **Notifications Center (G8)**: The display center for real-time (SignalR) alerts regarding bookings, status changes, or approvals.

### Phase 6: Admin Agent Workflow (Jointly Owned)
- **Agent Monitoring & Approval (G9)**: Implementing the `/admin/agent-workflow` surface. As per specs, this is a shared effort, but belongs in the general routing. It will display the tables and states of AI agent runs for Admin oversight.

## Verification Plan
### Automated Tests
- We will rely strictly on unit tests using vitest/react-testing-library (if available in this setup) for component rendering.

### Manual Verification
- Manually test routing for public vs. protected surfaces.
- Confirm layouts adapt as expected to role mocks (Customer vs. Provider vs. Admin).
